The $\lambda_E$ Euler evaluation of $(F_{n,\gamma}')_n$ is a number $b_{\sigma,\gamma}$ satisfying $$\label{pos:strict-bound}
 b_{\sigma,\gamma}
    \ge\nu_\sigma\eta_E
    \ge
       \frac{\lambda_D(U)}{\operatorname{length}_B(B/\mathfrak{m}_B^a)}
       \frac{r_E}{t_E}
    >0.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
Let $(D,\mathfrak d,k)$ and a chosen finite generically separable base $A\subseteq D$ be as in Lemma <a href="#len:normalization" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="len:normalization">4</a>, and let $\Lambda$ be the tower <a href="#len:tower-definition" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="len:tower-definition">[len:tower-definition]</a>. There is a $D$-algebra $C_D$, carrying a compatible $\Lambda$-action, such that restriction of scalars defines an additive nonnegative length $\lambda_D=\lambda_\infty$ on its modules annihilated by a power of $\mathfrak d$. For every parameter system $z_1,\ldots,z_h$ of $D$ and every integer $v\geq1$, $$\begin{aligned}
 \lambda_D H_i(z_1^v,\ldots,z_h^v;C_D)&=0\qquad(i>0),
                                      \label{len:koszul-vanishing}\\
 \lambda_D\bigl(C_D/(z_1^v,\ldots,z_h^v)C_D\bigr)
                    &=v^h e((z_1,\ldots,z_h),D).
                                      \label{len:parameter-length}
\end{aligned}$$ The right side is positive and finite. The algebra and length are independent of the parameter system $z$. For the regular parameters of $A$, in particular, $$\label{len:base-parameter-length}
 \lambda_D\bigl(C_D/(t_1^v,\ldots,t_h^v)C_D\bigr)
                         =v^h\operatorname{rank}_A D.$$ The finite-stage, infimum, and supremum properties of Lemma <a href="#len:tower" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="len:tower">5</a> remain available on underlying tower modules; they do not require that the relevant submodules or covers be $C_D$-modules.

There are finite-length $B$-modules $M_n$ and positive integers $s_n\to\infty$, with $\mathfrak{m}_B^aM_n=0$, such that $$\begin{aligned}
 \frac{\operatorname{length}_B(M_n)}{s_n}&\longrightarrow\lambda(U),
       \label{pos:approximation-length}\\
 \frac{\operatorname{length}_B\operatorname{Tor}_i^B(M_n,L)}{s_n}
       &\longrightarrow\tau_i(L)
       \quad(L=k,E',\ i\ge0).
       \label{pos:approximation-tor}
\end{aligned}$$ Writing $\beta_0(M_n)=\dim_k(M_n/\mathfrak{m}_BM_n)$, we also have $$\label{pos:generator-bound}
 \frac{\beta_0(M_n)}{s_n}\longrightarrow\nu_\sigma,
 \qquad
 \nu_\sigma\ge
 \frac{\lambda(U)}{\operatorname{length}_B(B/\mathfrak{m}_B^a)}>0.$$

The $\lambda_E$ Euler evaluation of $(F_{n,\gamma}')_n$ is a number $b_{\sigma,\gamma}$ satisfying $$\label{pos:strict-bound}
 b_{\sigma,\gamma}
    \ge\nu_\sigma\eta_E
    \ge
       \frac{\lambda_D(U)}{\operatorname{length}_B(B/\mathfrak{m}_B^a)}
       \frac{r_E}{t_E}
    >0.$$
